WEBVTT

00:00:00.155 --> 00:00:05.002
Standardization and correction should not be treated as the same operation.

00:00:05.002 --> 00:00:08.682
Trimming an email or changing case preserves the intended value.

00:00:08.682 --> 00:00:17.207
Mapping tech to Electronics may be appropriate if the business taxonomy explicitly defines that equivalence.

00:00:17.207 --> 00:00:23.497
Changing a negative price to a positive price makes a much stronger claim about reality.

00:00:23.497 --> 00:00:25.102
That kind of correction needs evidence.

00:00:25.102 --> 00:00:30.942
Connect this idea to a product catalog standardizing categories and quarantining invalid rows.

00:00:30.942 --> 00:00:36.557
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:36.557 --> 00:00:42.332
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:42.332 --> 00:00:49.877
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:49.877 --> 00:00:54.720
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
